.SH NAME
maknoon-completion-zsh - Generate the autocompletion script for zsh


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBmaknoon completion zsh [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Generate the autocompletion script for the zsh shell.

.PP
If shell completion is not already enabled in your environment you will need
to enable it.  You can execute the following once:

.EX
echo "autoload -U compinit; compinit" >> ~/.zshrc
.EE

.PP
To load completions in your current shell session:

.EX
source <(maknoon completion zsh)
.EE

.PP
To load completions for every new session, execute once:

.SS Linux:
.EX
maknoon completion zsh > "${fpath[1]}/_maknoon"
.EE

.SS macOS:
.EX
maknoon completion zsh > $(brew --prefix)/share/zsh/site-functions/_maknoon
.EE

.PP
You will need to start a new shell for this setup to take effect.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for zsh

.PP
\fB--no-descriptions\fP[=false]
	disable completion descriptions


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--fips\fP[=false]
	Enforce strict FIPS-140 compliant cryptographic standards

.PP
\fB--json\fP[=false]
	Output results in JSON format

.PP
\fB--passphrase-file\fP=""
	Read passphrase from a file instead of prompting (use - for stdin). Also settable via MAKNOON_PASSPHRASE_FILE

.PP
\fB--policy\fP=""
	Path to a declarative governance policy file (JSON)

.PP
\fB--tpm\fP[=false]
	Enable TPM 2.0 hardware-backed storage for keys

.PP
\fB--tpm-device\fP="/dev/tpmrm0"
	Path to the TPM device node

.PP
\fB--tpm-pcrs\fP=[]
	List of PCRs to bind keys to (e.g., 7,14)

.PP
\fB--trace\fP[=false]
	Enable low-level diagnostic tracing to stderr


